# Security, Validation, and Logging Guardrails

Authentication & Authorization
- Do not expose admin-only routes to unauthenticated or unauthorized users.
- Enforce role checks in controllers/filters; prefer CI4 Filters for route groups.

Input Handling
- Validate all user inputs with CI4 Validation rules ([app/Config/Validation.php](mdc:app/Config/Validation.php)).
- Escape output in views; avoid printing raw input.
- Use CSRF protection via Filters if forms mutate state ([app/Config/Filters.php](mdc:app/Config/Filters.php)).

Transport & Headers
- Review CORS/CSP in [app/Config/Cors.php](mdc:app/Config/Cors.php) and [app/Config/ContentSecurityPolicy.php](mdc:app/Config/ContentSecurityPolicy.php).

Error Handling & Logs
- Never echo stack traces in production views.
- Use CI4 Logger for server-side errors ([app/Config/Logger.php](mdc:app/Config/Logger.php)); logs go to [writable/logs](mdc:writable/logs).

Data Privacy
- Limit data exposure in JSON responses to the minimum required fields.
- Sanitize file uploads and store in [writable/uploads](mdc:writable/uploads).